# First-call state (LAYOUT-STARTUP-STATE-LOCALE-3, ruling #4942): what the first setlocale, setenv, localtime_r,
# mktime and catalog lookups touch, never a process that makes none of those calls. The zero-filled objects go to
# their own page-aligned cluster in `.lbss`, after `.bss` (xtask/src/coldbss.rs FIRST_CALL_SECTION): in `.data1`
# they lay between the every-process tier and the C members' start-up words, and the `true` probe touched one page
# more. Initialised ones (stdout, __tzname, ...) and those of another member than the Rust object stay in `.data1`,
# after the every-process tier. Every entry after the next line is first-call state; hot_text_products names any
# the `true` probe touches.
cluster first-call
# The first setlocale reads, then writes, the table counters and the secure-mode flag `process::secure`
# caches. LAYOUT-DATA-CLUSTERS-9: once program_invocation_name is in the cluster, start-up no longer touches
# the last `.bss` page, and the first of these left there costs setlocale a read and a write fault on it
# (setlocale + printf and tool +1 against next); declared one at a time, the faults moved to the next one
# (NAME_COUNT, then SECURE, then GENERATION and MAPS), so the set is declared together.
liella_legacy::global_locale::MAPS
liella_legacy::global_locale::COUNT
liella_legacy::global_locale::NAME_COUNT
liella_legacy::global_locale::FILE_COUNT
liella_legacy::global_locale::GENERATION
liella_legacy::global_locale::QUERY_SEQ
liella_legacy::global_locale::QUERY_HANDLE
liella_legacy::global_locale::QUERY_SLOT
liella_boundary::process::SECURE
# The catalog change counter the first setlocale bumps (LAYOUT-DATA-CLUSTERS-11): after next's merge it was that
# call's only write on the last `.bss` page start-up leaves untouched (one fault, setlocale + printf 51 -> 50).
symbol _nl_msg_cat_cntr
# The flag every close reads first (csys/src/machine/points.S; LAYOUT-SINGLE-FAULT-TEST): in the assembly member's
# shared `.data` the first close (the `rebind` probe's) read it on a page whose place followed emission order.
symbol liella_machine_aio_used
# The rest of what the first setlocale and the first printf to stdout touch (LAYOUT-STARTUP-STATE-LOCALE, #4915):
# left in `.bss`/`.data`, their page followed emission order, and setlocale + printf read 50 or 51 and tool 54 to
# 56 by `.bss` pad. hot_text_products `init_startup_data_accesses_are_in_the_data1_cluster` traces every probe.
liella::locale::collate::ASCII_KEYS
liella_legacy::intl::GENERATION
liella_legacy::intl::SETTINGS
symbol _IO_2_1_stdout_
symbol stdout
